<title>UK: GECC adds 10 bln drachma to March 1999 bond.</title>
<headline>GECC adds 10 bln drachma to March 1999 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following fungible issue was announced by lead manager SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   GENERAL ELECTRIC CAPITAL CORP</p>
<p> AMT  **10 BLN GRD    COUPON     9.50	MATURITY    17.MAR.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.925   PAY DATE ** 30.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.125     REOFFER    99.925    SPREAD	=</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (M) ONE	 SALE LIMITS US/UK/GR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  1.0	 PRAECIP     =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>	   ** FUNGIBLE WITH EXISTING 15 BLN DRACHMAN BOND LAUNCED</p>
<p>		24.FEB.97 AT 100.983, PLUS 133 DAYS ACCRUED INTEREST</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
